.TH ROLEDEL "8" "October 2026" "libnss-role" ""
.SH NAME
roledel \- Delete roles and remove priviledges from role
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B roledel
[\fI-m\fR] [\fI-f FILE.role\fR | \fI-S\fR] \fIROLE \fR[\fIGROUP\fR...]

.B roledel
\fI-r\fR [\fI-f FILE.role\fR | \fI-S\fR] \fIROLE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
roledel is utility allows to remove priviledges groups from role groups.
This mean that all users at role group excludes from all
privileges groups which removed from modified role.
.PP
By default \fI/etc/role\fR is changed. Roles from \fI/etc/role.d\fR are
changed with \fB\-f\fR or \fB\-S\fR option, see \fBrole\fR(5).
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR [ \fB\-\-help\fR ]
produce help message
.TP
\fB\-r\fR [ \fB\-\-remove\fR ]
remove role with all privilegies
.TP
\fB\-m\fR [ \fB\-\-skip\-missing\-groups\fR ]
skipping for missed privilegies instead error
.TP
\fB\-f\fR [ \fB\-\-file\fR=\fIFILE.role\fR ]
change role in additional file \fI/etc/role.d/FILE.role\fR
.TP
\fB\-S\fR [ \fB\-\-system\fR ]
change system role in additional file \fI/etc/role.d/ROLE.role\fR
.TP
\fB\-v\fR [ \fB\-\-version\fR ]
print the version of roledel being used
.SH FILES
\fI/etc/role\fR, \fI/etc/role.d/*.role\fR
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
.BR role (5),
.BR roleadd (8),
.BR rolelst (8)
